# pair-lmm-gwes v0.6.3

Standalone low-rank, h2-capped LMM pairwise pangenome GWES tool.

## v0.6.3 changes

- Preserves original PAN-GWES/SpydrPick pair-file metadata in `pair_lmm_gwes.tsv`.
  For a no-header pair file, columns are interpreted as:
  `u v distance ARACNE MI count M2 min_distance max_distance`.
- The general plotter supports PAN-GWES graph-count filtering with `--n`:
  `count >= ceiling(0.05 * n)` by default.
- The plotter can also merge PAN-GWES metadata from `--pairs` if the score table was generated by an older version and lacks `count`.
- Plot labels, axis text, and summary annotations are enlarged for easier viewing on smaller screens.

## Main commands

```bash
pair-lmm-gwes \
  --fasta fake_ac.fasta \
  --pairs pairs.ud_sgg_0_based \
  --out pair_lmm_gwes_results \
  --threads 32 \
  --min-count 10 \
  --grm-rank 0 \
  --grm-shrinkage 0.3 \
  --ctmc-11-mode posthoc \
  --tree-11-posthoc-score-threshold 7.55 \
  --tree-11-posthoc-distance-min 10000
```

Plot with the PAN-GWES graph-count filter:

```bash
pair-lmm-gwes-plot \
  --score pair_lmm_gwes_results/pair_lmm_gwes.tsv \
  --out pair_lmm_gwes_results/pair_lmm_gwes_plot.png \
  --y-col bidirectional_score \
  --threshold 7.55 \
  --ld-dist 10000 \
  --n 1337 \
  --ctmc-filter \
  --ctmc-filter-after-ld
```

If plotting an older result table that lacks the `count` column, also supply the original pair file:

```bash
pair-lmm-gwes-plot \
  --score old_pair_lmm_gwes.tsv \
  --pairs saureus.mi_filtered.ud_sgg_0_based \
  --out plot.png \
  --threshold 7.55 \
  --n 1337
```

`--n 1337` applies `count >= ceiling(0.05 * 1337) = 67` using the `count` column by default. Use `--pair-count-frac`, `--pair-count-min`, or `--pair-count-col` to override this behaviour.
